<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<odoo>
    <record id="tax_icms_regulation_search" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">l10n_br_fiscal.icms.regulation.search</field>
        <field name="model">l10n_br_fiscal.icms.regulation</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <search string="ICMS Regulation">
                <field name="name" />
            </search>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="tax_icms_regulation_tree" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">l10n_br_fiscal.icms.regulation.tree</field>
        <field name="model">l10n_br_fiscal.icms.regulation</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <tree>
                <field name="name" />
            </tree>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="tax_icms_regulation_form" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">l10n_br_fiscal.icms.regulation.form</field>
        <field name="model">l10n_br_fiscal.icms.regulation</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <form string="ICMS Regulation">
                <sheet>
                    <group>
                        <field name="name" required="1" />
                        <field name="icms_imported_tax_id" required="1" />
                    </group>
                    <!-- The state pages are added after the help page by
                         _apply_state_tax_definition_tabs (models/icms_regulation.py) -->
                    <notebook>
                        <page name="help" string="Help">
                            <div class="alert alert-info" role="alert">
                                <strong>The ICMS regulation is the table that answers:
                                "leaving state X for state Y, what is the ICMS?"</strong>
                                The ICMS of ordinary sales and purchases comes from
                                here, with nothing to configure per operation.
                            </div>
                            <ul>
                                <li>The internal and interstate rates of all the
                                states are already registered and maintained by the
                                community. Each state has its own tab, with the ICMS,
                                the ICMS ST, the FCP and the tax benefits.</li>
                                <li>State benefits (base reduction, exemption for
                                certain products) enter here as rules by state and
                                NCM.</li>
                                <li>Only <strong>approved</strong> rules apply. When
                                more than one fits, the tax benefit comes first, then
                                the specific rule of the NCM, CEST or product and,
                                last, the general rule of the state.</li>
                                <li><strong>Simples Nacional</strong> companies do not
                                use this table: their ICMS is paid in the DAS, with
                                the percentage of the annex and range computed on the
                                company.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert">
                                Changes here affect <em>all</em> the sales and
                                purchases of the companies that use this regulation.
                                When in doubt, confirm with your accountant before
                                changing.
                            </div>
                        </page>
                    </notebook>
                </sheet>
                <div class="oe_chatter">
                    <field name="message_follower_ids" groups="base.group_user" />
                    <field name="activity_ids" />
                    <field name="message_ids" />
                </div>
            </form>
        </field>
    </record>
</odoo>
